From 919d0b32c02a7d0aa9739473349c73ac5f63ec10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthias Clasen <mclasen@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:40:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] build: Don't promote unused globals to errors with clang

Clang 23 includes -Wunused-but-set-global in -Wunused-but-set-variable.
GLib type macros create parent-class globals that are legitimately unused
in some types, so Pango fails when the latter warning group is promoted
to an error. Keep the warning visible but do not make its global variant
fatal.

Based on a patch by David Nylander (!927).

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/pango/-/issues/900]
Signed-off-by: Ross Burton <ross.burton@arm.com>
---
 meson.build | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 9a5dc9ed1..58faa8496 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -148,6 +148,7 @@ elif cc.get_id() == 'gcc' or cc.get_id() == 'clang'
     '-Werror=empty-body',
     '-Werror=write-strings',
     '-Werror=unused-but-set-variable',
+    '-Wno-error=unused-but-set-global',
     '-Wundef', # FIXME: https://bugzilla.gnome.org/show_bug.cgi?id=792481
   ]
 
